==English==

===Etymology===
Coined in translation of [[w:François Rabelais|Rabelais]]' works, from {{bor|en|frm|matagrabolisme}}, from {{m|frm|matagraboliser||mystify}}. The first element is from {{der|en|grc|μάταιος||vain, futile}}, but altered to assimilate to the prefix {{af|en|meta-}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|humorous|rare}} [[concealment|Concealment]], [[mystification]], [[obfuscation]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1653|author=François Rabelais|title=Gargantua and Pantagruel
|passage=[A]ll the autonomatic '''metagrobolism''' of the Romish Church, when tottering and emblustricated with the gibble-gabble gibberish of this odious error and heresy, is homocentrically poised.}}

